{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-puzzle-solving", "file": "references/post-rejection-action-gate.md", "content": "# Gate the next action after rejection

A rejected submission provides only a binary signal; it does not identify which cells were wrong. Do not respond with a speculative near-variant based on the same demos. Revisit the complete model: output shape, transformation trigger, role/color mapping, changed-cell mask, and unchanged regions. If multiple materially different hypotheses remain and the demo budget permits, request a demo chosen to separate them. Submit again only when there is a specific evidence-based model revision that reproduces all demonstrations.

In this instance, two visibly different demo pairs showed localized changes: one recolored only selected 1-cells to 2 while other 8-cells remained, and another filled much of the region bounded by 8 while preserving boundary cells. A test guess that globally filled the region around the 3-cells was rejected. The demos did not validate that broad fill operation on the test; after rejection, the sound next move is targeted evidence gathering rather than arbitrary color or footprint changes.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-rnd0/frozen/seen/play/users/u046/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-puzzle-solving/references/post-rejection-action-gate.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-puzzle-solving", "file": "references/session-18868900-output-shape-review.md", "content": "# Session review: periodic lattice to compact output

This session is a cautionary example of under-validated transfer. Demos supplied repetitive stripe/lattice grids with compact outputs of several different dimensions (5×6, 2×4, 5×4, 3×2), while the test had a 28×27 periodic lattice. A small guessed grid based on salient marker cells was submitted without a demonstrated derivation of its dimensions or cell mapping; it was incorrect. A second answer likewise used an unvalidated extraction rule and was incorrect.

Reusable lesson: before transferring a periodic or lattice transformation, explicitly derive both (a) output dimensions and (b) the mapping from complete input units/coordinates to output cells, using every demo. Do not confuse a visually plausible marker subset with the actual extraction rule. After binary rejection, it is not enough to alter one edge or color: reassess shape and mapping together, and request a demo only when a specific competing mapping can be distinguished.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-rnd0/frozen/seen/play/users/u046/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-puzzle-solving/references/session-18868900-output-shape-review.md"}
